# What `vercel deploy` uploads when it is run from the REPOSITORY ROOT.
#
# ★ THE DEPLOY NO LONGER RUNS FROM HERE.
#
# `host-platform.sh` deploys from `static/` — the composed single-root tree that
# already holds the pages, the assets and the API bundle — because that is the
# only directory whose CONTENTS are the site. This file is kept for two reasons:
# a Vercel Git integration (if it is ever connected) deploys from the root, and a
# developer running `vercel` by hand from the root should upload the same thing.
#
# ★ A PRESENT `.vercelignore` REPLACES `.gitignore`, IT DOES NOT EXTEND IT.
#
# This file used to hold only two `!` re-includes. That was enough to get the
# generated `static/` tree into an upload, and it silently did the opposite for
# everything else: with no `.gitignore` in play, `node_modules/` was no longer
# excluded either, and an upload became 12,069 files and 1.2 GB. The CLI then
# failed with "Upload aborted" beside a truncated list of missing hashes — which
# reads like a network fault and is actually the file list.
#
# So every exclusion is stated here. `node_modules/` is the one that matters:
# Vercel installs it from `package.json` during the build, and the API function is
# a single pre-bundled file (`api/index.js`), so nothing needs it on the wire.

# Dependencies. Installed by the builder, never shipped from here.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Build output the builder produces, or that compose-static merges.
.expo/
.vercel/
.cache/

# Local and verification artefacts, which carry credentials and screenshots.
.verify/
.git/
.worktrees/
*.log
metro.err
metro.log

# Nothing outside the deployed surface needs to travel.
.github/
tests/
docs/
design/
supabase/
migrations/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Files Vercel must NOT skip.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ★ THE BUG THE `!` LINES EXIST FOR.
#
# `static/` is the composed single-root deploy tree, and it is generated. When it
# was filtered out of the upload the failure was asymmetric, which is why it read
# as a font bug rather than a deploy bug: the HTML in `static/` was small enough
# to have been published already, but every file under `static/assets/` 404'd —
# including all 24 font files. The browser reported success on the page and 404 on
# the typeface, so English text fell back to a system font and looked like a
# missing `fontFamily`.
#
# `!` re-includes a path an earlier rule would otherwise drop.
!static/
!static/**

# `dist/` is the raw Expo export that compose-static.sh merges into `static/`.
# The deploy must not depend on a previously committed copy of either.
!dist/
!dist/**

# The API function is committed as a bundle, so it must survive the excludes.
!api/
!api/**
